* ==========================================================================
* CPLEX option file 2 (FULL RUN): negcap2050 = A1 bio-CCS-realism + 2050 cap.
* Solver settings IDENTICAL to the uncapped A1 run (..._aaa_reduced_transcost)
* so capped-vs-uncapped is a clean A/B; the ONLY model difference is the
* EMI_POLNA 2050 net CO2 <= -82 Mt cap (data/EMI_POLNA.inc).
* Use with: gams ... --USEOPTIONFILE=2
* ==========================================================================

LPmethod  6
* Concurrent barrier + dual simplex (proven config; barrier wins on this LP).

advind 0
* No warm start. (advind 1 REJECTED on Nordic.)

predual -1
* Auto primal/dual transformation.

scaind 1
* Aggressive scaling RESTORED (2026-05-29). scaind 0 was a stopgap but solved too
* slowly (couldn't even clear 2030). The DURABLE fix is now the QPBSCORE row-scale
* (PB_ROWSCALE in base PB, enabled via --PB_ROWSCALE_ON=yes): it collapses the
* cross-category VGE_AGG coefficient spread AT THE SOURCE, so the matrix is well
* conditioned and fast aggressive scaling no longer over-/un-scales into the 2040
* status-5. Row-scale is lossless (f cancels -> IS_<CAT>.l physical). See
* PB_rowscale_STAGED.md + RF_KNOWN_ISSUES.md.

solutiontype 0
* Barrier + crossover (basic vertex). Required for correctness.

numericalemphasis 1
* More careful pivoting on the 25-OOM coefficient spread.

dpriind 2
* Steepest-edge dual simplex pricing (concurrent dual thread).

bardisplay 2
* Barrier diagnostics (Cholesky factor summary etc.); concurrent mode limits
* what is emitted, but harmless and kept identical to the uncapped A1 run.
